WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:07.500
Use Google or create an email account. Each account gets a private demo workspace.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:15.596
Start with sample invoices and purchase orders. Use synthetic documents only.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:25.396
Choose “Approve a valid invoice” first. “Use sample” selects the PDF; it does not submit it.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:33.468
Check the selected file, then click “Start workflow”. Scanned PDFs take longer.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:41.668
“Ready for approval” means validation passed. A person must still review the invoice.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:50.084
Check the vendor, duplicate history and PO balance. Expand a rule to read its reasoning.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:59.252
Review the extracted values and source excerpts. Use “Original PDF” to check the document.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:07.884
Add a meaningful note (at least 5 characters). Approve only after checking the evidence.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:17.532
Your signed-in identity and review note are saved in the audit trail. Choose Approve invoice to accept this sample.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:28.708
This sample uses sixty thousand rupees of a one hundred thousand rupees PO, leaving forty thousand rupees. Approval does not send payment.

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:38.444
Download all five PDFs and test instructions, or choose Use sample. Approve the valid invoice first.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:47.924
A renamed PDF still has the same vendor and invoice number. The duplicate is blocked and cannot be approved.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:58.316
Only 40,000 rupees remains after the first approval. This 45,000 rupee invoice exceeds it by 5,000.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:07.540
Even with a review note, unresolved checks prevent approval. Request a correction or reject the invoice.

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:16.852
The required-information check flags the missing invoice number. The system asks for correction instead of guessing.

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:25.700
Add a clear note and choose Request information. The decision is recorded without accepting the invoice.

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:35.060
The information request is saved. The invoice stays pending, and the accepted PO balance does not increase.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:46.988
Try the printed scan to explore OCR. Reusing invoice numbers affects results. All samples work without ERPNext.
